From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Olivet <jordanolivet@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 22:47:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: guard off-thread block-entity access during light
 propagation

Light propagation runs on scalablelux-* worker threads. Block occlusion
shape, light-block opacity and light-emission lookups passed the real
Level to block methods; a block (e.g. TreeChop's ChoppedLogBlock) could
then call getBlockEntity() and force-load a neighbour chunk off the main
thread, throwing "Should always be able to create a chunk!" which wedges
shutdown and freezes the JVM.

Route those queries through a new LightSafeBlockGetter backed by the
non-forcing lighting chunk view (LightChunkGetter#getChunkForLighting),
returning null/air when a chunk is not loaded for lighting instead of
force-creating it off-thread. Cached per lightAccess on the engine.

